Warn on each SPIR-V compile emitted unoptimized because spirv-opt cannot be loaded.

When slang-glslang (which carries spirv-opt) cannot be loaded, the SPIR-V back end
(source/slang/slang-emit.cpp) emits the module unoptimized and unvalidated, and getEntryPointCode
returns SLANG_OK. Session::getOrLoadDownstreamCompiler (source/slang/slang-check.cpp) reports the
failed load, as E00100 "failed to load downstream compiler 'spirv-opt'", an error, with a note per
library tried, and only on the session's first attempt, because the attempt is remembered. A host
therefore sees an error diagnostic on a successful result for its first compile, and nothing at
all for every later one, whose modules are just as unoptimized: 1,280 bytes against 992 for one
shader measured, 22.5 % larger.

This loads spirv-opt for optimization and validation without the load's diagnostics, and when it is
unavailable warns E00118 spirv-optimizer-unavailable on every compile it affects. A compile that
must link several SPIR-V modules cannot proceed without the library and keeps the load's
diagnostics. The behaviour needs the library to be absent, so it is not covered by a unit test;
the measurement below copies an application without slang-glslang.

Measured on v2026.14.1 (win-x64), two SPIR-V compiles in one global session without slang-glslang:
E00100 on the first, nothing on the second. The patched behaviour is measured on v2026.21.
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-diagnostics.lua b/source/slang/slang-diagnostics.lua
index 8aab09cee..6d707d02d 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-diagnostics.lua
+++ b/source/slang/slang-diagnostics.lua
@@ -589,6 +589,12 @@ err(
 
 err("failed-to-load-downstream-compiler", 100, "failed to load downstream compiler '~compiler'")
 
+warning(
+    "spirv-optimizer-unavailable",
+    118,
+    "the SPIR-V was emitted without optimization or validation: 'spirv-opt', which is in the 'slang-glslang' library, could not be loaded"
+)
+
 err(
     "downstream-compiler-doesnt-support-whole-program-compilation",
     101,
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-emit.cpp b/source/slang/slang-emit.cpp
index 4dc7e9058..5dc441679 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-emit.cpp
+++ b/source/slang/slang-emit.cpp
@@ -3632,11 +3632,18 @@ static SlangResult createArtifactFromIR(
     artifact->addRepresentationUnknown(
         needsDownstreamCompiler ? ListBlob::create(spirv) : ListBlob::moveCreate(spirv));
 
+    // Optimization and validation are optional: the module is valid without them. A missing
+    // optimizer is therefore not an error of the compile that cannot load it, which reports success,
+    // and the session reports a failed load only on its first attempt. Each compile it affects warns
+    // instead. A link cannot happen without the library, so that case keeps the load's diagnostics.
+    //
     IDownstreamCompiler* compiler = needsDownstreamCompiler
                                         ? codeGenContext->getSession()->getOrLoadDownstreamCompiler(
                                               PassThroughMode::SpirvOpt,
-                                              codeGenContext->getSink())
+                                              needsLink ? codeGenContext->getSink() : nullptr)
                                         : nullptr;
+    if (!compiler && needsDownstreamCompiler && !needsLink)
+        codeGenContext->getSink()->diagnose(Diagnostics::SpirvOptimizerUnavailable{});
     if (compiler)
     {
